<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Stucco repair in Calgary starts with a diagnosis, not a trowel. A hairline crack, a patch of hail pocking, a bulge over the garage and a hollow spot beside a window can look alike from the driveway and need very different work. This page walks through how an independent stucco contractor sorts them, what a patch can and cannot do, and what Calgary firms publish for prices.</p><p>Sandstone Stucco Co is an advertising service paid by independent contractors. It puts homeowners in Calgary, Airdrie, Chestermere, Cochrane and Okotoks in touch with them, and the contractor who quotes your job contracts directly with you. This site does no stucco work itself. Call (403) 555-0148 and describe the wall, or see the <a href="/stucco-repair-cost-calgary/">stucco repair cost guide</a> for more figures.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Hairline versus structural cracks</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Imasco, a stucco manufacturer, says some cracking is inherent to portland cement and is not a reflection of product quality. Ask the contractor where the crack starts, how wide it is and whether it has moved.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Patches and holes</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Martini Stone Masonry lists one back-wall repair as flashing, paper, mesh, two coats of mortar and a matched texture. Calgary Parging lists small patch repairs at $550 to $1,125 before GST.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Bulges and delamination</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Calgary Parging lists bulge repair, such as above a garage, at $1,450 to $3,000 before GST. Calgary Stucco and Slate notes that nobody can name the full extent of water damage until the wall is opened up.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Windows, doors and the base of the wall</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Martini Stone Masonry says temperature movement opens 3 to 8 mm gaps where stucco meets frames, and that piled snow softens the lowest 12 to 18 inches of a wall. Calgary Parging lists window and door repairs at $975 to $3,000 before GST.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Colour and texture match</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Imasco, a stucco manufacturer, says colour can vary with weather, texture, job conditions and method of application. Ask the contractor how close a patch will get before work starts.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Repair or recoat</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Total Exteriors, a Calgary contractor, suggests repair when damage is localized and moisture is minimal. The call is the contractor's, made after seeing your wall.</p>
      </div>
</div>
